Hi,
read.GenePix  reads in the data from a genepix gpr file row by row.
Genepix gpr files have a standard nesting order
of:
Columns nested within Rows nested within Blocks. 

If the nesting order from a third party gal file gene list is different
and you use read.marrayInput on the gal file associated
with multiple gpr files then your annotations Names and ID's will not
match your gpr data.
Since one gal file will generally be associated with many gpr data
files, you just need to make the nesting order the same so the 
genes match the data, or run read.marrayInput on one of your gpr data
since the Names and ID's are also in the gpr datafile 
in the correct order.

marcus

